{
  "_about": [
    "What a child types, and what they meant.",
    "",
    "The catalogue is written in the words of a librarian: CODING, ART, REFERENCE.",
    "A child types 'make a game', 'drawing', 'minecraft'. Without this file the",
    "search on notsus.net finds nothing for either, and a filter that finds nothing",
    "is worse than no filter, because the child concludes the site is empty.",
    "",
    "Written 2026-11-06 for docs/WEBSITE-REPLICA-PRD.md. Needs a second pass once",
    "real children have typed into it: the terms below are a guess at what they say,",
    "and some of them will be wrong.",
    "",
    "Covers all 106 active sites. Checked against docs/catalog/featured.json, which",
    "is generated from the catalogue, so a site added or removed there shows up here",
    "as a site with no synonyms or a synonym with no site.",
    "",
    "How it is used: a search matches a site if the typed words appear in its name,",
    "its description, or any term listed for it here or for its category. Matching",
    "is case-insensitive and on word stems, so 'draw' catches 'drawing'."
  ],

  "_rules": [
    "Lower case, no punctuation.",
    "Include misspellings children actually make, not every possible typo.",
    "Include brand names children ask for by name, even ones we do not carry,",
    "  where we have an honest alternative. 'minecraft' pointing at Tinkercad is",
    "  a fair answer to 'I want to build things'. It is not a claim to be Minecraft.",
    "Never map a brand we do not carry to something unrelated just to fill a gap.",
    "British and American spellings both."
  ],

